Sources were selected from https://science.ecosyste.ms/projects/codemeta_csv on
2026-09-26. The listing contained 1,936 repository URL and file path pairs.
Selection took the first six rows and every 64th row, followed by targeted
CodeMeta, generator, sourmash, and fairgraph sources. Missing files are recorded
in acquisition-failures.json, rather than excluded from the acquisition record.

Each occurrence records its repository, source path, commit, blob ID, and SHA-256.
Files are copied without changes. Equal byte sequences share one local fixture,
including matches with the upstream and comparison corpora. Original authors
retain ownership; each source repository provides its licensing terms.

Fourteen occurrences run in the compact corpus. CODEMETA_CORPUS=all includes
all occurrences. The sample includes context versions 2.0, 3.0, and master;
unsupported and mixed contexts; Role wrappers; scalar agents; non-ASCII names;
nested dependency objects; and malformed JSON. No cached science file matched
a literal root-graph key search. The pinned upstream context supplies a real
root-graph document, with synthetic cases covering graph traversal separately.

Parse outcomes are separate from context detection and diagnostics. Metadata is
compared against encoding/json with UseNumber, and original bytes are checked
against their hashes. Unresolved classifications identify cases whose reported
range or context differences have not established upstream invalidity. They do
not label every file with a diagnostic invalid. Malformed JSON was also rejected
by Ruby's JSON parser. Defaults accommodate the acquired sample without resource
or diagnostic truncation.
